## Immutable Configuration Trade-off

### Enable Global Immutability

```go
app := fiber.New(fiber.Config{
    Immutable: true, // All context values become immutable
})
```

### ⚖️ Trade-offs

**✅ Benefits:**
- All context values safe to use anywhere
- No need to manually copy values
- Prevents data corruption bugs

**❌ Costs:**
- **Significant performance penalty**
- Defeats Fiber's zero-allocation design
- Higher memory usage per request

### When to Use

- ✅ Development/debugging
- ✅ Prototyping
- ✅ Low-traffic applications
- ❌ **Production high-throughput APIs**
- ❌ Performance-critical systems

